method.writingBody:
Weekly summaries are written with artificial intelligence, following precise rules:
- use only information found in the source article, without adding figures, dates, names or facts;
- report figures exactly as in the source, stating the period and area they refer to;
- write in plain Italian suited to 12-16 year olds, explaining acronyms;
- end with a «Why it matters to you» paragraph linking the news to students' choices, without inventing data.

Every AI-written summary says so next to the text. The English version, when available, is a translation of the same texts.
